**What a SYN flood attack actually is**:
SYN packets keep sending bursts of protocol messages while waiting for ACK responses. A server with open connection ports (5673 in port 80/443) will sit there patiently, flooding the server behind it. The number of bytes sent is measured in packets per second, reaching hundreds to millions per machine.

